### 4. Login certo → 200 + token (salva o token numa variável)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hemerson@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaForte123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refresh", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 5. Senha errada → 401
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hemerson@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaErrada999"
}

### 6. E-mail que não existe → 401 com a MESMA mensagem
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ninguem@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaForte123"
}

### 7. /me sem token → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me

### 8. /me com token → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Token adulterado → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### 10. Refresh → 200 com tokens NOVOS (guarda o antigo para o teste de roubo)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("refreshAntigo", client.global.get("refresh"));
    client.global.set("refresh", response.body.refreshToken);
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### 11. Reusar o refresh ANTIGO → 401 (simula o ladrão; revoga tudo)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshAntigo}}" }

### 12. Tentar o refresh NOVO → 401 também (o roubo derrubou a família inteira)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### 13. Logout (rode o 4 de novo antes, para ter um refresh válido) → 204
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### 14. Refresh depois do logout → 401
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }